From 333c45ac485681f718f381f85775d3a03ae2f75d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rawdanger-recomp <rawdanger-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:13:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rd: frame generation moves things that are not characters
 (v0.10.8)

Each step keeps the depth-writing 3D batches, brought into the world with the step's
matrix, matched with the same batch a step before; a rigid move (Horn's fit) becomes a
thing (box + matrix back) in the bones buffer, and interp.wgsl moves the pixels inside
it to the moment shown. Rain, sprites, corners at the eye and things cut at the picture's
edge are left out. Settings > Debug: switch, view, log; PS2_FRAME_GEN_OBJECTS[_VIEW|_LOG|_TEST].

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
